description:
Effective written communication is the ability to communicate ideas, information, and perspectives clearly, adapting a message to different audiences and situations, and using the appropriate style to convey meaning in various written contexts.

By completing the course associated with this badge, students will demonstrate information literacy, comprehension of written material, and conveying information in writing for a variety of rhetorical purposes and audiences. Some of the learning outcomes associated with the college course that results in this badge include: 
• Examining and analyzing written material; 
• Synthesizing information and ideas;
• Developing content relevant to the purpose. 
• Demonstrating the ability to write to a specific audience. 
• Presenting a perspective informed by research and critical thinking. 
• Revising written communication based on feedback. 

Importance in Workplace: 
• Enhances an employee’s ability to interpret and evaluate a wide variety of written material;
• Promotes research, critical thinking, and problem solving;
• Advances the development of clearly written material relevant to the intent;
• Enhances the use of appropriate language for the intended audience;
• Increases the competent, effective, and responsible use of information.

criteria.narrative:
# Competencies

Learners successfully completed the courses associated with the following set of competencies: 

1) Demonstrate project management techniques over the life cycle of a data analysis process

2) Architect an end-to-end business strategy to power analytic insights

3) Defend a business strategy intended for executive leadership

4) Implement a technical analytic strategy for approaching a complex business problem 

5) Complete a multi-stage analytics problem collaboratively by separating it into discrete action items

6) Create technical documentation of methodology and implementation associated with an end-to-end business strategy

These competencies are made up of essential skills, which are demonstrated through hands-on projects assessed with rubrics. 

# Skills

Successful completion of these projects shows that learners have acquired these skills: 
Data Analysis - Clean, format, and combine data to assess its appropriateness for answering business questions;

Research - Develop exploratory business strategy questions based on available datasets; Research - Find, evaluate, and organize datasets that can be used to address business problems; 

Business Intelligence - Use analytics processes and techniques to provide insight into business strategy and operations; 

Communications - Propose data-informed recommendations to executive stakeholders; 

Teamwork - Collaborate with colleagues on an end-to-end analytics project; 

Problem-Solving - Develop an approach for solving a multi-stage analytics problem; 

Project Management - Track deliverables and progress when solving complex business problems; 

Writing - Document the technical approach used to address a complex business problem; 

Planning - Outline processes for solving technical problems in business contexts."

Learners successfully completed the courses associated with the following set of competencies: 

**1)** Develop KPIs that align to business strategy

**2)** Apply appropriate data visualization tools and techniques for communicating data analysis results

**3)** Present visual solutions that provide value to end-users and decision-makers

 **4)** Create insight oriented visualizations using industry tools, 

**5)** Clean data by applying appropriate tools and techniques without adversely affecting data integrity

**6)** Integrate various visualizations to articulate data-driven narratives to both technical and non-technical audiences.

These competencies are made up of essential skills, which are demonstrated through hands-on projects assessed with rubrics. Successful completion of these projects shows that learners have acquired these skills: 

**Data Analysis -** Clean, format, and combine data to assess its appropriateness for answering business questions

**Research -** Develop exploratory business strategy questions based on available datasets; Research - Find, evaluate, and organize datasets that can be used to address business problems; 

**Tableau -** Construct interactive data visualizations and dashboards in Tableau to help answer strategic business questions; 

**Business Intelligence -** Develop meaningful business insights by analyzing complex datasets related to business metrics; 

**Communications -** Produce business stories with interesting insights, actionable ideas, and clear visuals; 

**Problem Solving -** Package visualizations into compelling decision-making tools; 

**Detail Oriented -** Exercise attention to detail to identify anomalies and errors in data that could impact data integrity; 

**Organizational Skills -** Use automated correction techniques to efficiently complete data processing tasks; 

**Presentations -** Present complex data visualizations to stakeholders to inform business strategy.

This badge is awarded to students who demonstrated empirical and quantitative skills and were evaluated at a level of proficient or higher on the following:  

-Defining and contextualizing a problem statement; 

-Developing and applying an approach to analyze and address the variety of quantitative and qualitative information available; 

-Considering the appropriateness of the data provided and collected while also evaluating data for biases; 

-Synthesizing results of data analyses in a clear and relevant manner that is related to the problem statement at hand, and;  

-Interpreting results of data analyses to formulate valid explanations, inferences, and to present relevant conclusions.

This badge is awarded to students who demonstrated teamwork and were evaluated at a level of proficient or higher on the following:  

- Collaborating to develop goals, plans, and timelines for the benefit of the group; 

- Contributing to group outcomes by completing tasks and supporting other group members with a high level of excellence; 

- Facilitating the growth and improvement of the team by encouraging contributions from all, providing constructive feedback as appropriate, and supporting members who are not engaging regularly; 

- Supporting team climate and culture by treating team members with respect, maintaining a positive attitude, and encouraging the team to strive towards the goal at hand, and; 

- Directly addressing feedback and/or conflict to strengthen team culture.

