Students in this activity complete all course requirements while having an opportunity to practice:
- describing a problem or question comprehensively;
- examining a question with evidence and efficacy;
- considering context, assumptions, and the credibility of all perspectives and sources;
- justifying one's own argument;
- and, presenting a logical and coherent conclusion.

This badge is awarded to students who demonstrated critical thinking and were evaluated at a level of proficient or higher on the following:  

- Describing the issue/problem clearly and with relevant information; 

- Questioning and selecting evidence by evaluating source credibility and developing an analysis to support thinking; 

- Considering one's own assumptions and those of others with the intent of considering context and bias when presenting a position; 

- Justifying one's own position while taking into account the complexity and nuances of an issue; and, 

- Presenting conclusions, related implications, and consequences based on available analysis and evidence.

